+# Read Models Carry Derived Page State
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The specialty directory lists every specialty with the veterinarians holding it. The stored model runs the other way. `Vet` owns the many-to-many association, and `Specialty` carries no back-reference. Producing the page therefore inverts the association and orders both levels.
+
+No page in the codebase derives its state this way today. Every controller passes repository results to the view unchanged, or pages them. `docs/architecture-principles.md` admits no business rule in a web controller, and records that the existing controller rules are a deviation which new rules do not extend.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Group inside the controller** — `VetController` reads both repositories and builds the grouping inline. Matches the prevailing style of the upstream sample.
+2. **Invert in a query** — a join over `Specialty` and `Vet` returns the pairs. Moves the traversal into the repository.
+3. **Read model in the feature package** — an immutable type built from the stored specialties and veterinarians, holding the inversion and the ordering.
+
+## Decision
+
+Derived page state lives in a read model: an immutable type in the feature package, built by a static factory from what the repositories return. The controller reads, delegates, and selects the view.
+
+Option 1 adds a fresh rule to a controller. Option 2 expresses the inversion as a query the unidirectional mapping does not support cleanly, and the default suite would exercise it against H2 alone.
+
+A read model is not a service layer. It holds no dependency, opens no transaction, and is built from values its caller already has. [Feature-Package Organization Without a Service Layer](2026-07-31-feature-package-organization.md) stands unchanged.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The inversion and the ordering become unit-testable with real `Vet` and `Specialty` objects, without MVC infrastructure.
+- The controller keeps to the *Web controller* row of the pattern catalog.
+- The codebase gains a type shape it did not have. A reader of the upstream sample finds it unfamiliar.
+- Reads stay whole-collection, so each request rebuilds the read model over data the vet cache already holds.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the type registry the read model joins
+- [architecture-principles.md](../architecture-principles.md) — the *Web controller* row this decision keeps
+- [system-design.md § Open Questions from the Survey](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey) — the service-layer question this decision leaves open
